{"id":"sw-e87204","type":"CREATE","payload":{"description":"## Sandbox Crate (`crates/sandbox`)\n\nA standalone binary for developing and testing the engine. Replaces the current `crates/viewer` as the primary way to exercise engine features during development.\n\n### Scope\n\n- **Crate scaffold** — move current viewer, worldgen, and model_gen code here. Depends on `smallworld-engine`. The viewer becomes a sandbox, not a product.\n- **Test scenes** — switchable scene presets: terrain-only, objects-only, stress test (thousands of instances), single-brick debug, empty world. Hot-key or egui dropdown to switch.\n- **Engine integration smoke tests** — exercises each engine system as it lands (audio playback, UI widget gallery, field visualization, etc.)\n\n### Separation principle\n\nThe sandbox is a **developer tool**, not a game. It exists to:\n- Validate engine features in isolation\n- Profile and benchmark rendering paths\n- Provide a visual testbed for new systems before the game crate wires them up\n- Demonstrate the engine's integration API for future users\n\n### Relationship to Game Crate\n\nThe game crate builds a product; the sandbox builds confidence. Both depend on the engine, neither depends on the other.","labels":["epic","tooling"],"sort_order":"b0G","status":"BACKLOG","title":"Sandbox Crate: dev/test harness for engine integration"},"created_at":"2026-08-06T06:56:40.833491Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.222 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"sw-4a1fc0","type":"CREATE","payload":{"description":"## Field Simulation\n\nA generic framework for propagating scalar values through the voxel world. The engine provides the solver; the game defines what the fields mean.\n\n### Scope\n\n- **Scalar field storage** — per-brick float channel, sparse (only allocated where the field is active). Multiple named fields can coexist (heat, moisture, toxicity, etc.)\n- **Diffusion solver** — per-tick propagation step on active bricks. Configurable diffusion rate, dissipation, boundary conditions. Runs in job system workers.\n- **Field query API** — read/write field values at world positions. Exposed to scripting runtime so game scripts can react to field state.\n- **Source/sink primitives** — engine-level concept of field emitters (torch → heat) and absorbers (water → heat sink). Game defines which objects are sources/sinks.\n\n### Use cases (game-layer)\n\n- **Heat**: fire spreads to wood, melts ice, cooks food. Visual: emissive glow on hot voxels.\n- **Moisture**: rain accumulates, drains downhill, affects terrain (mud). Visual: wet surface shading.\n- **Toxicity/gas**: poison clouds propagate, dissipate over time. Visual: fog tint.\n- **Electricity**: wire-like propagation for redstone-style mechanics.\n\n### Technical direction\n\nActive-set approach: only bricks with non-zero field values (or adjacent to them) participate in the tick. Bricks settle to zero and drop out of the active set. This keeps cost proportional to active area, not world size.","labels":["epic","engine","simulation"],"sort_order":"b0H","status":"BACKLOG","title":"Field Simulation: generic scalar propagation on the brick grid"},"created_at":"2026-08-06T06:56:49.737952Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.222 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"sw-ff12d4","type":"CREATE","payload":{"description":"Rename/refactor `crates/viewer` into `crates/sandbox`. Move worldgen and model_gen into the sandbox crate (they're test content, not engine). Update workspace Cargo.toml, Makefile targets. Engine crate retains only core systems — no test scene code.","estimate":3,"labels":["feature","tooling"],"parent_id":"sw-e87204","sort_order":"b0I","status":"BACKLOG","title":"Sandbox scaffold: move viewer/worldgen/model_gen into crates/sandbox"},"created_at":"2026-08-06T06:56:57.212879Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.222 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"sw-73f01a","type":"CREATE","payload":{"description":"Scene preset system. Each preset defines world setup (terrain params, object placement, camera start). Presets: terrain-only, objects-only, stress test (1000+ instances), single-brick debug, empty world. Switchable via egui dropdown or hot-key. Supports adding new presets as engine features land.","estimate":3,"labels":["feature","tooling"],"parent_id":"sw-e87204","sort_order":"b0J","status":"BACKLOG","title":"Switchable test scenes: terrain, objects, stress, debug"},"created_at":"2026-08-06T06:56:59.991485Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.222 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"sw-480d26","type":"CREATE","payload":{"description":"As each engine system lands (audio, UI, fields, etc.), add a sandbox scene or panel that exercises it. Audio: play test tones with spatial positioning. UI: widget gallery showing all primitives. Fields: heat source visualization. Keeps the sandbox as the go-to proof that each system works end-to-end.","estimate":2,"labels":["feature","tooling"],"parent_id":"sw-e87204","sort_order":"b0K","status":"BACKLOG","title":"Engine integration smoke tests: visual testbed per system"},"created_at":"2026-08-06T06:57:03.583286Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.222 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"sw-48380b","type":"CREATE","payload":{"description":"Per-brick float array (one value per voxel), allocated on demand. Multiple named fields can coexist. Active-set tracking: only bricks with non-zero values are in the active set. Bricks that settle to zero are deallocated and removed from the active set. Sparse — cost proportional to active area, not world size.","estimate":3,"labels":["feature","engine","simulation"],"parent_id":"sw-4a1fc0","sort_order":"b0L","status":"BACKLOG","title":"Scalar field storage: sparse per-brick float channels"},"created_at":"2026-08-06T06:57:06.406313Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.222 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"sw-d9a57d","type":"CREATE","payload":{"description":"Per-tick diffusion step across active bricks. Configurable per field: diffusion rate, dissipation (decay per tick), boundary conditions (solid voxels block, air passes). Handles cross-brick boundaries. Runs in job system workers for parallelism. Source/sink primitives: emitters add value, absorbers remove.","estimate":5,"labels":["feature","engine","simulation"],"parent_id":"sw-4a1fc0","sort_order":"b0M","status":"BACKLOG","title":"Diffusion solver: per-tick propagation on active bricks"},"created_at":"2026-08-06T06:57:09.307407Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.222 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"sw-862bc2","type":"CREATE","payload":{"description":"API to read/write field values at world positions. Bulk queries for regions. Exposed to scripting runtime so game scripts can read temperature at a position, set a heat source, query moisture for terrain effects, etc. GPU upload path for visualization (e.g. heat-map overlay in sandbox).","estimate":2,"labels":["feature","engine","simulation"],"parent_id":"sw-4a1fc0","sort_order":"b0N","status":"BACKLOG","title":"Field query API: read/write values, script bindings"},"created_at":"2026-08-06T06:57:12.242602Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.222 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
