{"id":"sw-e4bdd6","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"Per-preset camera paths for benchmark harness","description":"Replace the generic orbit camera in `--bench` mode with per-preset camera paths that exercise each scene's interesting geometry. Each `Preset` provides a `camera_path(t: f32) -\u003e (Vec3, f32, f32)` where `t` is normalized progress 0..1. The bench module calls this instead of its own orbit logic.\n\nExamples:\n- **Default**: orbit that dips to canopy level, rises to overview\n- **Terrain Only**: sweep along terrain surface through valleys\n- **Objects Only**: weave between objects at eye level\n- **Stress**: pull back for overview, push in close\n- **SingleBrick**: tight orbit at brick scale\n- **Empty**: static camera (nothing to see)","status":"DOING","parent_id":"sw-e87204","estimate":2,"sort_order":"a0","assignee":"Claude Code \u003cagent@macbook.local\u003e","labels":["feature","tooling"]},"created_at":"2026-08-06T07:54:14.00448Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.222 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
