{"id":"sw-1b7156","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-d41d61aa-2aac-4eb7-a010-edad43219e5d","text":"## Summary\n\nAdded SSE-driven traversal termination to the raymarcher.\n\n**Modified files:**\n- `crates/engine/src/raymarcher.rs` — added `focal_length` and `sse_threshold` to `Uniforms`, `sse_threshold` parameter on `render()`\n- `crates/engine/shaders/raymarch.wgsl` — added `focal_length`/`sse_threshold` to uniform struct, `sample_brick_lod()` function, SSE checks in both `trace_terrain` and `trace_object` before `trace_brick`\n- `crates/sandbox/src/main.rs` — added `sse_threshold` to `RunState`, egui slider (0.0–4.0), passes threshold through to `render()`\n\n**How it works:**\n- `focal_length = render_height / (2 * tan(fov_y / 2))` computed per frame\n- Before entering the fine DDA: `sse = voxel_size * focal_length / distance`\n- If `sse \u003c threshold`, skip fine DDA and shade from `sample_brick_lod()` (probes center + 3 fallback positions for a representative color)\n- If all probes are air, lets the ray continue (doesn't force a hit on empty bricks)\n\n**Rationale:** \"Never do sub-pixel work\" — at 1080p with 10cm voxels, full resolution only needed within ~90m. Beyond that, individual voxels are invisible; tracing them wastes cycles.\n\n**Decisions made:**\n- SSE distance uses ray t-parameter (distance along ray) rather than Euclidean camera distance — cheaper and directionally correct\n- For objects, distance is converted to world space via `rd_scale` before SSE computation\n- Default threshold 1.0 px; slider range 0.0 (disabled) to 4.0 (aggressive)\n- `sample_brick_lod` returns `vec3(-1)` sentinel for all-air bricks to avoid false hits\n\n**Status:** fmt, clippy, 29 tests, smoke all pass. Ready for review."},"created_at":"2026-08-06T08:09:17.388862Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.222 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"sw-81d536","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"Consolidate render flags into engine-side RenderSettings struct","description":"Replace the growing parameter list on `Raymarcher::render()` (flags, sse_threshold, ...) with a single `RenderSettings` struct in the engine crate. Games and sandbox each own an instance, wire it to their UI, and pass it to render. One parameter instead of N.","status":"PLANNED","parent_id":"sw-d6d2c2","estimate":2,"sort_order":"ap","labels":["feature","engine"]},"created_at":"2026-08-06T08:30:05.063095Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.222 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
